WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.408
Timer App turns any meeting or workshop into a full screen countdown that everyone in the room can read.

2
00:00:06.408 --> 00:00:09.447
Every countdown starts with a two step setup.

3
00:00:09.447 --> 00:00:14.376
Step one collects the details, and step two picks how the clock animates.

4
00:00:14.376 --> 00:00:15.926
Name the countdown first.

5
00:00:15.926 --> 00:00:24.480
The description is required, capped at eighty characters with a live counter, and it follows the timer all the way through to the summary.

6
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.813
Then set the length in hours, minutes and seconds.

7
00:00:27.813 --> 00:00:32.880
Each field takes digits only and clamps itself to a valid range as you type.

8
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.746
You can also write the message the timer celebrates with at the end.

9
00:00:36.746 --> 00:00:39.816
Leave it blank and it falls back to a plain Time's Up.

10
00:00:39.816 --> 00:00:43.489
Once a countdown is running, the clock takes over the screen.

11
00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:47.825
The timer is stored in the browser, so closing the tab does not lose it.

12
00:00:47.825 --> 00:00:53.064
Here is a fifteen minute standup that was paused with thirteen and a half minutes left.

13
00:00:53.064 --> 00:00:56.256
Resume picks it up from exactly where it stopped.

14
00:00:56.256 --> 00:01:04.488
While it runs, the screen keeps only what matters: the name of the session and digits big enough to read from the back of the room.

15
00:01:04.488 --> 00:01:11.904
Underneath the clock you get the start time, the projected finish, a progress bar and the percentage already elapsed.

16
00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:17.832
A toggle in the corner pushes the whole timer into fullscreen for a projector or a second display.

17
00:01:17.832 --> 00:01:23.640
Pause freezes the remaining time, and Cancel clears the session and returns you to setup.

18
00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:29.024
Step two of setup picks how the clock animates, and four styles ship with the app.

19
00:01:29.024 --> 00:01:31.848
Default pops each digit card as it changes.

20
00:01:31.848 --> 00:01:34.752
Slide rolls the digits over like an odometer.

21
00:01:34.752 --> 00:01:40.560
Fade blurs one digit into the next, and flip is the hinged flip clock you saw a moment ago.

22
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:46.848
When the clock reaches zero the timer celebrates with confetti and the custom message you wrote during setup.

23
00:01:46.848 --> 00:01:53.040
A summary card logs the date, when the session started and ended, and the total time it was scheduled for.

24
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:58.344
One click clears everything and drops you back at setup, ready for the next session.
